WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:06.550
When you work for the SCP Foundation, one
certainty is that nothing – no turn of events,

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.500
no scenario – is ever really unexpected.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.730
No matter how unlikely something may appear,
chances are it usually happens.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:20.600
And if it doesn’t happen here, then in an
infinite multiverse of alternatives, everything

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.359
than can possibly happen is statistically
likely to.

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:29.580
We’ve covered a few of these alternate eventualities
before, a number of which revolve around the

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:39.629
differing events in the long life of one particular
anomaly: SCP-076-2, better known as Able.

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:45.010
In our own home universe, much like he is
in many others, Able is considered to be a

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.640
near-perfect warrior.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:52.290
His body, covered in tattoos of occult symbols
and demonic faces, is capable of withstanding

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.010
vast amounts of physical damage.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:01:00.399
Able can easily take hits from the most powerful
conventional weapons mankind has to offer,

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:02.980
and survive with little more than a scratch.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.110
What’s more, he can draw an endless supply
of black-bladed weapons from a tiny pocket

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:09.110
dimension.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:14.619
And on top of all that, even in the event
that he’s bested in combat, Able’s body

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:22.400
will rapidly disintegrate, only to reform
within a large stone cube known as SCP-076-1.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.259
Like most of us, Able has a number of almost
identical counterparts that exist across the

00:01:27.259 --> 00:01:29.560
various worlds of the multiverse.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:34.990
One of them once had the opportunity to reconcile
with his brother Cain, the man seemingly responsible

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:37.200
for Able’s endless life of bloodshed.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.350
And once the two brothers had made peace,
they could rest.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.579
In another universe, Able worked directly
with the SCP Foundation as part of a Mobile

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:48.650
Task Force, until they turned on him.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:54.560
This unfurled a chain of events so cataclysmic
that the entire world would suffer the consequences.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.149
This alternate Able went on the warpath against
the Foundation, ultimately using SCP-914,

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:04.960
the Clockworks, to refine his destructive
anomalous abilities.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:10.610
This allowed him to unleash chaos, slaughtering
all of humanity in an omnicide that wiped

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:15.640
the world clean of all other life, leaving
Able sat alone in a dead world.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.569
And then there was this version of the immortal
warrior.

00:02:18.569 --> 00:02:24.020
Far from the Clockworks enhanced conqueror
that his alternate universe counterpart was,

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:30.290
this Able had long since been removed as a
member of MTF Omega 7, and was gradually reconstituting

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.780
his body within SCP-076-1.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:39.129
His most recent defeat had enraged the warrior,
and he had vowed to once again be free.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.629
Although, unbeknownst to him, what set this
particular version of Able apart from his

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:49.569
other variants was the fact that he would
soon encounter a certain other anomaly.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:55.810
Something that, when wielded by SCP-076-2
had the potential to… completely rob him

00:02:55.810 --> 00:03:00.370
of all his centuries’ worth of fighting
ability and replace it with an embarrassment

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.420
that would last for centuries more.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.290
But first, a quick history lesson.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.950
Much like it had been in our universe, this
particular anomalous object had been recovered

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:15.110
by the Foundation after it made its way into
the hands of an unwitting police officer.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:21.290
The item in question was SCP-572, a particularly
unique katana.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:25.370
Unique in that it was utterly useless for
fighting with, and caused more harm to the

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.500
person wielding it than whoever they were
trying to use it against.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.480
In this universe, the sword had already changed
hands a number of times.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.150
When police were called to the home of one
Clarence ‘Clancy’ Clancerson, he drew

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:43.890
SCP-572 in defense and screamed at the officers
that he would “take their heads, and with

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.010
it, their power.”

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:49.510
The cops, who had been sent over to arrest
Clancy for violent and disorderly behavior,

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:53.980
were less than threatened to see their suspect
– who was somewhat out of shape – coming

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.220
at them with a weapon no sharper than a butter
knife.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:02.090
After pacifying Clancy with tasers and beanbag
rounds from a twelve gauge shotgun, the police

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:07.590
retrieved SCP-572, and it was then acquired
by a Foundation operative.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.209
This all played out almost the exact same
way in our universe.

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:15.310
However, in this version of events, there
was one key difference.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:22.940
As previously mentioned, SCP-572 was an unremarkable
sword, but it had something of a storied past,

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.820
passing from one unfortunate user to the next.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.480
And just as it has recovered from Clancy’s
house and ended up in Foundation hands, one

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.889
of those former owners had just been about
to reclaim the fabled weapon for himself…

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:40.380
Meanwhile, back in this containment chamber,
deep under the ocean, still trapped in the

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.100
stone cube he reanimated within, Able was
lost in a dream.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:49.610
To any other person, falling asleep to see
subconscious visions of so much carnage would

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:53.020
be horrifying; they’d call it a nightmare.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.650
But to Able, this might have been one of the
sweetest dreams he had ever experienced.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:03.650
All around him was a world on fire, having
returned to life once again, Able had at last

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.430
bested his captors at the SCP Foundation.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:13.070
In his dream, he had traveled the world, visiting
every Foundation facility one by one and reducing

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.440
them to rubble, without leaving a single survivor.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:22.050
Then, once the work was done, he turned his
barbarism towards the wider world, and began

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:25.009
slaughtering humanity in droves.

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:29.910
Perhaps some distant cosmic echo had reached
out across the multiverse, a fragment of the

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:35.979
life of a more refined version of himself
had slipped into Able’s subconscious, making

00:05:35.979 --> 00:05:41.430
him dream that he, too, was the omnicidal
conqueror that his other self was.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:46.509
Seeing such devastation in his own wake made
this version of Able eager to wake up, to

00:05:46.509 --> 00:05:53.470
revive once more and set about making this
delightful dream of destruction a deadly reality.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:57.850
It was while Able was dreaming, picturing
himself cutting down all who dared to oppose

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.710
him, that something strange seemed to happen.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:01.730
He had a visitor.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.620
Not a visitor to his containment chamber,
mind you.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:10.210
There was no one beyond the confines of SCP-076-1
except the security team that normally kept

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.670
the stone cube under armed surveillance.

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:19.940
No, this visitor appeared somewhere else:
inside Able’s mind, approaching him as he

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:20.940
slept.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:24.840
Within the warrior’s slumbering fantasy,
he was climbing up a mountain of skulls after

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:28.479
having slaughtered millions – if not billions
– already.

00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:33.039
But as he reached the top of the pile of bones,
and looked out over the horizon, Able could

00:06:33.039 --> 00:06:35.440
see that the world beyond was still living.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.349
There were just as many people alive, perhaps
even more than he’d already killed.

00:06:40.349 --> 00:06:45.410
His work was not yet done – in fact, it
seemed that despite all the lives the immortal

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:49.160
madman had already claimed, he had barely
even begun.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:52.260
“Oh, Able,” a voice tutted.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.889
“Did you really think you could do it alone?”

00:06:55.889 --> 00:06:59.610
Even though this was a dream, Able could feel
the presence of another.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:03.759
He pulled one of his obsidian-edged weapons
from thin air and swiped in the direction

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:06.389
the voice had come from, hitting nothing.

00:07:06.389 --> 00:07:12.199
The blade in his hand seemed to change, its
dark metal transforming from solid to liquid.

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:17.240
Coming apart in his hands, Able’s sword
melted like candle wax under a hot flame,

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.770
reduced to nothing in seconds.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.900
“You can’t do it,” the voice whispered.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.789
“You aren’t strong enough.

00:07:23.789 --> 00:07:25.930
But I can help with that.”

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:30.310
Pulling home another weapon, a two-handed
axe this time, Able looked around him, trying

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.590
to locate the source of the taunting noise.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:38.090
“Only a coward relies on cheap tricks and
illusions!” he growled angrily.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.090
“Show yourself!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.610
Come forward and be slain!

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.430
Are you a worthy opponent?

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.210
Are you worth your time?”

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.770
“Are you?”

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.080
the voice jested.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.150
“We shall see!”

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.150
Able yelled.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.490
Behind him, a cloaked figure silently appeared.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:57.090
They looked to be adorned in a robe that whipped
in the biting cold wind, yet their garments

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.470
weren’t made of any fabric.

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:03.430
Instead, they wore a robe made out of pure
shadow, their clothes and body comprised of

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.880
the same thing.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.509
Though they lacked any tangible, solid matter,
it didn’t stop Able from spinning around,

00:08:09.509 --> 00:08:12.500
swinging his heavy axe in the figure’s direction.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:16.330
Before the blade of the weapon was even halfway
through the air, it had already started to

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:19.539
become liquid – just like the swords had
earlier.

00:08:19.539 --> 00:08:24.090
By the time it came down to strike at the
shadowy visitor, what had once been an axe

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:28.830
was just a flick of melted black metal, passing
through the intangible specter as Able found

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.750
himself once again unarmed.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:36.890
“Speak, cretin!” he demanded, never one
to back away from a fight, even when his weapons

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.380
were seemingly failing him.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:40.090
“Tell me who you are.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:43.690
I would know my adversary’s name before
I end your worthless life.”

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:47.860
“I’m not here to fight you,” the figure
replied calmly.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:52.170
“I’m here to offer you the key to your
victory, Able.”

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.730
“What key?”

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:54.810
the warrior sneered.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.480
“What could you possibly give me?”

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:02.470
“Exactly what you need to finish it,”
the shadow replied, drawing something from

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.930
a sheath on its belt and holding it aloft.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:10.290
“A weapon that will allow you to become
the conqueror you long to be.”

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.700
Able looked at the object in the figure’s
outstretched hand: a katana.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.190
Or at least, the shadowy vestige of one.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:17.600
“A sword?” he sneered.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.810
“What use do I have for a sword?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:23.490
I can conjure all the blades I need at will!”

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:28.630
To demonstrate, Able pulled one of his own
black blades, but yet again it began to melt

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.630
away.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:34.050
“Your weapons have served you well, but
they are disposable,” the shadow explained.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.500
“A true warrior deserves a sword worthy
of his fighting prowess.”

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:43.649
“I have killed scores of men through the
ages,” the immortal warrior retorted.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:47.040
“And I never needed any special sword to
do that!”

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:52.779
“And that is why, no matter how many you
kill, you will always be beaten.”

00:09:52.779 --> 00:09:56.810
In his dream, Able paused a moment, looking
at the katana and considering.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.779
Then, he reached his hand out to grip the
shadowy hilt.

00:09:59.779 --> 00:10:06.550
In that same split second, SCP-076-2 awoke
once again from his slumber and broke free

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:08.510
of the stone cube encasing him.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:15.010
As he killed his way through the Foundation
personnel in the facility housing SCP-076-1,

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:19.170
Able had only one thought in his mind: he
needed that sword.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:24.710
You see, what the immortal maniac was unfortunately
totally unaware of, was the interesting effect

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:27.990
SCP-572 could have on people.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:32.750
As well as being a totally useless sword,
anyone who picked it up will instantly believe

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:37.730
the Katana of Apparent Invincibility to be
an all powerful weapon of ancient legend.

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:42.910
Despite the sword being crudely made, blunt
and generally unfit for any use, the wielder

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:47.640
will maintain the belief that it not only
has perfect balance and cutting power, but

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:53.930
that the sword has also imbued them with unparalleled
strength and invincibility to damage.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:59.329
And now, either through the sword itself extending
this cognitohazardous influence into Able’s

00:10:59.329 --> 00:11:04.360
dream, or by the interference of some unknown
trickery, one of the most dangerous anomalous

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:10.800
killers in the world was making a beeline
straight for SCP-572… and he wasn’t the

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.250
only one either.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:18.300
At a previous point in time, a man by the
name of Zac had purchased SCP-572 on ebay.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:23.209
But it was far more than just an oddity to
him, he wasn’t looking to start a sword

00:11:23.209 --> 00:11:24.209
collection.

00:11:24.209 --> 00:11:28.570
As a child, he had been obsessed with comic
book superheroes, and when Zac bought that

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:34.030
katana, he intended to use the blade to dispense
vigilante justice against those who preyed

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:35.500
on the innocent.

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:40.910
And even before he held it in his hands, Zac
too had felt the anomalous pull of the katana,

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:46.850
knowing in his heart it was the perfect weapon
to transform him into a hero.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:50.890
Of course, he had quickly been disproven when,
on his first night of crimefighting, Zac had

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:55.709
been hit by a mid size sedan in a multi storey
parking lot and suffered a concussion.

00:11:55.709 --> 00:12:00.550
Sent to the hospital and then charged with
attempted assault, Zac had long since lost

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:06.120
any and all interest in ever donning his costume
– comprised of hockey pads and a ski mask

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.959
– or picking up the sword ever again.

00:12:08.959 --> 00:12:14.019
But as time had gone on, that old familiar
pull had started to gnaw at Zac, urging him

00:12:14.019 --> 00:12:18.760
to get back in the superhero game; forgetting
how poorly that had worked out for him last

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:19.760
time.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:24.190
One problem still stood in his way though:
he needed his trusty sword back.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:28.680
Of course, in the time since he’d hung up
his hero outfit, Clancy had gotten his hands

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.680
on SCP-572.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:35.440
And then, right before Zac could steal it
back, the Foundation had taken it.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.220
It had taken him months of preparation.

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:41.960
He’d sneakily made dealings with a janitor
that worked at one of the Foundation sites.

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:47.380
Zac had bribed the man a lot of money in exchange
for his key card and uniform, even having

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:51.960
to take out a second mortgage on his apartment
to meet the frankly extortionate amount the

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.600
janitor asked for.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:58.860
But it would be worth the cost, Zac told himself;
if it reunited him with his trusty katana

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:01.000
then it’d be worth it.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.980
Only then would he once again be a full hero.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:08.839
Shuffling through the facility, Zac dragged
a mop over the floor, leaving a sign to warn

00:13:08.839 --> 00:13:09.990
of the slippery hazard.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:15.320
He whistled to himself, trying to act as casually
as possible, not realizing that he was slightly

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:16.320
overselling it.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:20.320
Once he was certain the coast was clear, he
made his move.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:26.140
SCP-572 was locked in a secure deposit box
within Site 19’s High-Value Item Storage

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:28.839
Facility, right where he had been cleaning.

00:13:28.839 --> 00:13:34.550
He began searching through the various anomalous
oddities kept there, until he saw it: the

00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:37.010
box containing his coveted sword.

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:42.180
All his effort in infiltrating the Foundation
had finally paid off, it was all leading to

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:44.550
this, his comeback to crimefighting…

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:49.160
It was at this precise moment that Able came
bursting through a nearby door.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:54.060
Completely befuddled, Zac quickly found himself
thrown to one side by the much stronger man.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.399
“Out of my way, weakling!”

00:13:56.399 --> 00:14:01.130
Able roared, before turning to face the deposit
box holding SCP-572.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:05.410
Gripping the box, Able used his superhuman
strength to tear it open as though the container

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.209
was made from carboard.

00:14:07.209 --> 00:14:12.860
There it was: stored safely within was the
weapon he had been seeking, the same all-powerful

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.300
sword from his vision.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:17.600
“At last,” he declared, reaching for the
hilt.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.190
“The sword belongs to me!”

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:25.390
The second that Able hoisted it into the air,
he felt a human weight dash towards him, only

00:14:25.390 --> 00:14:27.420
to shrug it off as it made impact.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.850
Zac tumbled to the floor, winded as Able barely
flinched at the attempted tackle.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.500
“You fool!” he roared.

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.120
“You dare come at me?

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:41.390
You’ll be the first to fall to my new blade,
the first of this pathetic world of unworthy

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:44.130
opponents to die in my conquest.”

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:49.160
Zac frightenedly raised his arms in an attempt
to shield himself, while Able raised the sword

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:50.720
menacingly above his head.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:55.269
The mortal man knew what that sword was capable
of… or so he thought.

00:14:55.269 --> 00:14:59.870
As Able brought the blade swiping downwards,
its true ineffectiveness as a melee weapon

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.550
was on full display.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:07.790
SCP-572’s dull, poorly balanced blade barely
grazed Zac’s arms as he protected his face,

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:11.230
in fact, beyond the initial swat, it barely
hurt.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:16.250
“I-I don’t understand,” Able stammered,
looking at the katana in confusion.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:20.220
“This is meant to be a warrior’s blade,
a weapon of champions and conquerors.”

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:24.620
“Yeah, that’s what I was thinking,”
Zac replied, also suffering from SCP-572’s

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:29.779
congntio hazardous effect – he’d fully
expected to die a second ago, slain by the

00:15:29.779 --> 00:15:32.050
very weapon he had been hoping to reclaim.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:34.829
“Still, maybe it’s just because it’s
your first go?

00:15:34.829 --> 00:15:38.779
I could show you how to-”
“Silence, I won't fall for that!”

00:15:38.779 --> 00:15:39.779
Able interrupted.

00:15:39.779 --> 00:15:42.180
“Let me see here, maybe the angle was off?

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:45.250
Or how about I use both hands, here let me
just…”

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:49.380
Once again, Able hoisted the weapon, this
time with both hands tightly gripping the

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:53.420
blade, intending to bring it slashing down
in a big swing like a woodsman cleaving a

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.079
log in two.

00:15:55.079 --> 00:15:59.690
Unfortunately, as he raised the sword, the
blade caught an exposed light fixture above.

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:03.910
Sparks burst from the ceiling as an electrical
current shot through the metal, and gave Able

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:05.010
a nasty shock.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.010
“Ouch!

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:09.410
What is the meaning of this?” he shouted
in frustration.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:13.649
“I’ve been alive for centuries, killed
thousands upon thousands of men since the

00:16:13.649 --> 00:16:14.649
dawn civilization.

00:16:14.649 --> 00:16:16.720
Why can’t I use this sword?!”

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:22.790
“Well, performance issues in a guy your
age, hardly an uncommon problem,” Zac joked.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.649
Both turned at the sound of a door being kicked
open, the clomp of heavy boots on the ground

00:16:26.649 --> 00:16:28.750
as a Foundation security team burst in.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:33.350
“SCP-076-2, drop your weapons and-” the
commander stopped mid-shout.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:37.019
“Wait, that’s not one of his regular swords,
is it?”

00:16:37.019 --> 00:16:41.390
“Sir, that’s…” one of the officers
paused and sighed.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:44.310
“I think that’s SCP-572.”

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.509
“Attack me!”

00:16:46.509 --> 00:16:50.400
Able yelled at the Foundation officers, pointing
the dull tip of the katana at them.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.590
“If you dare!

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:55.960
For I now wield the greatest blade known to
the universe!

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:59.010
You will all fall in a single stroke of my
new weapon.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.639
And once you have fallen, so shall the world!”

00:17:01.639 --> 00:17:08.049
“SCP-076-2 – Able, look – just put that
thing down,” the commander urged.

00:17:08.049 --> 00:17:10.350
“Trust me, you’ll thank yourself.”

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:14.950
“Pah, you pathetic fools are so afraid of
the chaos I will unleash!”

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.089
the warrior declared.

00:17:16.089 --> 00:17:18.000
“Such unworthy opponents!”

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.220
“Okay, I’ve seen enough,” the security
commander sighed.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.270
“Deadly force authorized.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.179
Light him up, boys.”

00:17:25.179 --> 00:17:31.150
On the commander’s signal, a hail of gunfire
erupted, bullets raining down on Able.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:35.500
He slashed SCP-572 through the air, certain
that what he thought was a mighty sword could

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:37.799
easily cut through the oncoming bullets.

00:17:37.799 --> 00:17:44.299
Of course, that may have been true, if SCP-572’s
only real power was not having any power at

00:17:44.299 --> 00:17:45.299
all.

00:17:45.299 --> 00:17:49.860
Each shot struck Able center mass, barely
damaging him given his body’s natural resilience

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:53.070
to harm, particularly from such small arms
fire.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:57.000
Although, he didn’t find it any less annoying
that he couldn’t seem to properly wield

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.070
his new katana.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:00.720
“Oh, are you kidding me?” he huffed to
himself.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.049
“What is with me today?

00:18:02.049 --> 00:18:05.710
Can’t get the hang of this thing; come on,
Able, it’s still a sword.

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:10.250
The weapon that will allow me to conquer this
whole world, but if I can just get the swing

00:18:10.250 --> 00:18:11.250
right…”

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:14.900
Calmly, knowing that the weapon itself posed
no threat – even in the hands of an immortal

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:19.340
mass murderer – the security team moved
in to apprehend Able.

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:23.450
Before they could take the katana from his
hands, he dashed towards them, swiping the

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:28.650
sword back and forth, hoping to hit at least
someone to get the ball rolling on his omnicidal

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:29.650
rampage.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:35.669
Instead, thanks to the influence of SCP-572,
he miscalculated, took a wrong step, and slipped

00:18:35.669 --> 00:18:41.309
over on a patch of freshly-mopped tile, landing
in a heap next to a ‘Wet Floor’ sign.

00:18:41.309 --> 00:18:46.340
The security team all winced, feeling the
secondhand embarrassment practically radiating

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:52.590
off Able as the ancient anomalous warrior
lay on the floor after a spectacular fall.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:56.890
Then, one by one, they all burst out into
uncontrollable fits of laughter.

00:18:56.890 --> 00:19:01.580
But while they were distracted, they were
completely oblivious to Zac, who emerged from

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:05.831
his hiding place and picked SCP-572 up off
the floor.

00:19:05.831 --> 00:19:10.400
He breathed a sigh of relief, reunited with
his prized weapon; having forgotten the severe

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:12.700
injury it caused him last time.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:13.700
“You…”

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:16.950
Able wheezed, still lying in a puddle of mop
water.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:18.510
“Who are you?”

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:23.230
Zac gave a slight smile, unzipping the janitor’s
overalls he had on to reveal a set of hockey

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:24.530
pads underneath.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:28.530
He slipped a ski mask over his face before
turning back to able and replying, in his

00:19:28.530 --> 00:19:31.970
most epic voice:
“I’m Captain Katana.”

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:36.411
Unfortunately, his return to crime fighting
would be as short-lived as Able’s own turn

00:19:36.411 --> 00:19:38.690
with SCP-572.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:43.780
As Captain Katana found himself hit by a bus
on his way home after trying to use the Katana

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:49.120
of Apparent Invincibility to cut said bus
in half down the middle… and failing in

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.549
a rather painful fashion.

00:19:51.549 --> 00:19:53.120
Want an anomaly of your own?

